        ⭐ WHAT THE ROW MEANS ONCE THIS IS GREEN. qalculate-qt's 4-of-11 is
           not the bundle leaking. Qt autolaunches a session bus, cannot find
           dbus-launch at /sbin or /bin, and falls back through a SHELL the
           environment supplies -- so the residue belongs to a process the
           application asked for and the bundle never carried.
        ⛔ WHICH FOUR ROWS ARE CLEAN IS REPORTED, NOT PREDICTED. The obvious
           story -- musl ships a static busybox, so the exec costs nothing --
           is FALSE: readelf says /bin/sh is a dynamic PIE on all eleven,
           alpine's busybox included. Q2 records that refutation so no
           later session repeats the guess.
        ⛔ AND IT IS A BUILD FLAG, NOT A PATCH: --with-program dbus-daemon
           dbus-launch puts the launcher in the artefact, the shell fallback
           is never reached, and the row closes at 11/11.
        ⚠ ONE subject. It explains this row; it does not revalidate the
           other twenty-five, and it does not say a bundle can never leak.

